# #58: Now Playing's snapshot must follow the track's database entry when
# it arrives after the snapshot. A song chosen from a list pushes Now
# Playing at once; the first snapshot can copy the placeholder id3
# (tagcache_idx 0, rating 0) that TRACK_CHANGE installs before the track's
# load copies the real one over it with no seq move. np_pb_entry_moved()
# notices (np entry id=.. tc=0 -> N) and the screen re-snaps the same track
# (identity: track id; validity: the entry), so the stars, the
# audiobook/podcast class and the rating target are right from then on.
# Here: the song is rated 3 stars, a second song is started from the list
# (fresh snapshot race), then the first song is chosen again: its stars
# show, and the rating written while the race window was open lands on the
# right file. Before the fix the same-track re-snap left the screen's
# rating at the placeholder's 0: the info stars stayed stale until some
# other redraw and the Rating page started from no stars (the owner's
# "stars keep disappearing").
#   SIM_BUILD=build/sim-ui scripts/shots.sh tests/ui/ipodui-fb-np-entry.script
# needs: library
# trace: np
# golden: skip first_rated again_stars again_rating
# log: np rating tc=18 stars=3 ok
# The re-snap line ("np entry tc=18 stars=3") appears only when the race
# is hit; since #109 queues by index the third play's snapshot usually
# has the entry already, so the stars are checked on again_stars instead.
wait 4000
wait_db 30000
sim_clock 15:08
key SELECT          # Music
wait 800
wheel +1            # Artists
wait 400
key SELECT
wait 800
wheel +5 300        # The Bellwethers
wait 1500
key SELECT
wait 800
wheel +1            # Flock Together
wait 400
key SELECT
wait 800
key SELECT          # first song: Now Playing pushes at once
wait 300
key SELECT          # Scrubber
wait 300
key SELECT          # Rating, right away (the race window)
wait 200
wheel -6 100        # 0
wheel +3 300        # 3 stars
wait 300
key SELECT          # rated: Normal, committed
wait 1200
shot first_rated
key MENU            # back to the album
wait 800
wheel +1            # second song
wait 400
key SELECT
wait 1500
key MENU
wait 800
wheel -1            # the first song again
wait 400
key SELECT
wait 1500
shot again_stars    # 3 stars
# leave the database as found
key SELECT
wait 300
key SELECT          # Rating: the row starts from the 3 stars
wait 600
shot again_rating
wheel -6 100
wait 300
key SELECT
wait 1500
audio_stop
quit
